# Explicit Types for Non-Obvious Local Variables

**Rule:** When a local variable's type is not obvious from the right-hand side (results of conditionals, `.first`, `.firstWhere`, nullable expressions), declare the type explicitly (including `?` when nullable) instead of relying on `final`/`var` inference. This makes the code self-documenting and avoids accidental wrong inference (e.g. `dynamic` or an unexpected supertype).

### ❌ Bad Example
```dart
final firstTicket =
    (tickets != null && tickets!.isNotEmpty) ? tickets!.first : null;
```

### ✅ Good Example
```dart
final TicketModel? firstTicket =
    (tickets != null && tickets!.isNotEmpty) ? tickets!.first : null;
```
